urnham defends axing triple lock with direct message to GB News viewers worried about pensions", "url": "https://www.gbnews.com/politics/andy-burnham-triple-lock-state-pension-gb-news", "summary": "Andy Burnham has defended his decision to reform the triple lock on state pensions with a direct message to GB News viewers concerned about their pensions and the cost of social care.The Prime Minister, who confirmed Labour will include changing the pension protection scheme in its next manifesto, was challenged directly by GB News Political Editor Christopher Hope over concerns the move could leave pensioners worse off.The triple lock currently guarantees that the state pension rises each year by whichever is highest of average earnings growth, inflation or 2.5 per cent.The cost of the policy has risen significantly beyond its original expectations, with the Office for Budget Responsibility estimating the triple lock will add £15.5billion a year to state pension spending by 2029-30 — around three times the £5.2billion it originally expected it to cost.TRENDINGStoriesVideosYour SayMr Burnham’s plans would move away from that system from April 2030, meaning the state pension would co...", "published_at": "2026-09-30T16:00:03+00:00", "image_url": "https://www.gbnews.com/media-library/image.png?id=68001885&width=1200&height=600&coordinates=0%2C50%2C0%2C50", "source": {"name": "GB News", "tier": "international", "url": "https://www.gbnews.com"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 80, "sensationalism": 13, "opinion_fact": 14, "factual_rigor": 70, "framing": 8, "confidence": 0.81, "rationale": {"lean": {"keyword_score": 50.0, "framing_shift": 0.0, "entity_shift": 0.0, "sentence_direction": 0.0, "text_score": 50.0, "source_baseline": 80, "text_shift": 0.0, "delta_max": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "top_left_keywords": [], "top_right_keywords": [], "framing_phrases_found": [], "entity_sentiments": {}, "state_affiliated": false, "unscored": false}, "sensationalism": {"headline_score": 1